# tools/al/ales_stereo_wav_witness.rish — two bounded i16 channel buffers round-trip through the canonical interleaved RIFF/WAVE
# stereo container, verify-before-trust (ALES216).
#
# Season: the Six-Season double-seat, Season C thread (Lotus · the creative suite) · waymark ALES · rung ALES216.
# Design read: active-designing/date/20260815/20260815-130649_fill-ales216-lotus-stereo-wav.md
# Idiom kin: lotus/wav.rye (ALES215) — the same canonical header and two-gate verify-before-trust decode, widened to two
# channels (channels 2 · block align 4 · byte rate rate*4) with samples stored interleaved L R L R, and one widened border:
# the data chunk must be a whole number of two-sample FRAMES, so neither channel ever receives a lone unpaired sample.
#
# lotus/stereo_wav.rye encodes two equal-length mono i16 buffers into the interleaved stereo RIFF/WAVE layout and decodes it
# verify-before-trust. The selftest proves: both channels round-trip byte-for-byte with the sample-rate field preserved; the
# payload is exactly L R L R; an empty pair yields a valid 44-byte header; a torn frame refuses PartialFrame at the frame
# border; and every header corruption — including a MONO container offered to the stereo decoder — refuses by name. A byte
# container only — no real file, no DAC, no acoustic or electrical fact asserted, no network, no keys, no funds, no real device.
#
# Run from the repository root:
#   rishi/bin/rishi run tools/al/ales_stereo_wav_witness.rish

say "ales-stereo-wav: Language EN — ALES216 closes the container's mono→stereo pair: two channel buffers encoded into the interleaved RIFF/WAVE stereo layout another program will play, and de-interleaved back verify-before-trust exactly as ALES215's mono container proved its samples whole."
say "ales-stereo-wav: Style Radiant — the same canonical 44-byte header, differing only where stereo differs (channels 2 · block_align 4 · byte_rate rate*4); every corruption refuses by name before a sample crosses."
say "ales-stereo-wav: Lens TAME — decoding is two independent gates, the size chain proving the container self-consistent and the frame border proving it frame-aligned so neither channel receives a lone unpaired sample; the sample rate is a carried field not a real clock; siloed to lotus/, no real file, no DAC, no network, no keys, no funds, no real device."

let zig = "vendor/zig-toolchain/zig"
let bin = "lotus/bin/stereo_wav"

let build = run ["sh" "-c" "mkdir -p lotus/bin && env RYE_ZIG=${zig} rye/bin/rye build lotus/stereo_wav.rye -femit-bin=${bin}"]
assert build.ok else "ales-stereo-wav: build failed — ${build.err}"

let outfile = "lotus/bin/stereo_wav.out"
let selftest = run ["sh" "-c" "${bin} selftest > ${outfile} 2>&1"]
assert selftest.ok else "ales-stereo-wav: selftest exited non-zero — see ${outfile}"

let shown = run ["sh" "-c" "cat ${outfile}"]
say "ales-stereo-wav: ${shown.out}"

let green = run ["sh" "-c" "grep -q 'GREEN ales-stereo-wav' ${outfile} && echo yes"]
assert (trim green.out) == "yes" else "ales-stereo-wav: selftest did not print the GREEN ales-stereo-wav line"

say "ales-stereo-wav: GREEN — the container family stands whole for mono and stereo; the next Lotus rung can carry a render that runs an effect chain over a buffer and writes the .wav result."
